+# Browser Control MCP
+
+This extension gives an agent a single, simple control track for a visible
+Chrome window on Windows:
+
+1. Call `observe_browser`
+2. Use the returned screenshot as the coordinate space
+3. Call `click_browser`, `drag_browser`, `scroll_browser`,
+   `type_browser_text`, `press_browser_keys`, or `open_url_in_browser`
+4. Call `observe_browser` again to verify the result
+
+The design goal is "act like a person using the browser", not "call lots of
+browser-internal APIs". It works on browser chrome and page content because it
+acts on the real visible window.
+
+## Tools
+
+* `list_browser_windows`
+* `observe_browser`
+* `click_browser`
+* `drag_browser`
+* `scroll_browser`
+* `type_browser_text`
+* `press_browser_keys`
+* `open_url_in_browser`
+* `wait_for_browser`
+
+## Coordinate model
+
+All point-based actions use **window-relative pixels**. The top-left corner of
+the screenshot returned by `observe_browser` is `(0, 0)`.
+
+That means:
+
+* if the browser moves, coordinates from an old screenshot are stale
+* if another app covers the browser, the screenshot will show that, just like a
+  human sees it
+* if you need reliable control, observe again after every important action
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+vpython3 agents/extensions/install.py add browser-control
+```
+
+## Quick check
+
+```bash
+vpython3 agents/extensions/browser-control/server.py --list-windows
+vpython3 agents/extensions/browser-control/server.py --self-test
+```
+
+For local debugging, the same two checks also work with plain `python` because
+the server has a lightweight fallback mode for non-MCP self-tests.
+
+## Current limits
+
+* Windows only
+* The browser window must be visible on screen
+* This is intentionally a minimal human-style control layer, not a full DOM or
+  DevTools abstraction
+* Observe, click, drag, and key-combo actions were validated against a real
+  Chromium window
+* Plain webpage text entry still needs one more hardening pass on some Chromium
+  content surfaces; the next upgrade should be a hybrid path that keeps the
+  same external MCP tools but uses CDP for webpage text/input when available
